# Secrets — MUST stay out of history.
#
# Why this file exists SEPARATELY from the rebuild-root .gitignore:
# `community/` is destined to become its own standalone (public) repository.
# The moment `git init` runs *inside this folder*, the rebuild-root .gitignore
# one level up stops applying and protects nothing. This file is what travels
# with the repo. Do not delete it, and do not rely on the parent's copy.
#
# `apps/api/.env` currently holds real third-party credentials reused from v1
# (GitHub OAuth, ORCID, Slack, OpenRouter, Telegram bot). The first commit is
# the point of no return: anything committed cannot be removed without
# rewriting history AND rotating every credential.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*.crt

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
.next/
out/
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Runtime artifacts and local data
apps/api/data/
**/apps/api/data/
dump.rdb
*.log

# Test / coverage output
coverage/
.vitest/

# Scratch / throwaway agent scripts. Never publishable.
# `apps/api/scripts/_tmp_allflags.ts` (which flips every boolean in the settings
# catalog to true, with no confirmation and no environment guard) and
# `_tmp_release.ts` were both sitting untracked-but-uningnored, so a first
# `git add -A` would have committed them into the public repo's history.
_tmp*
**/_tmp*
*.scratch.*

# Orphaned agent worktrees (created by an Agent-tool call with
# isolation: "worktree" that didn't get cleaned up) — a full nested clone
# with its own .git, found sitting untracked-but-unignored at 10MB.
.claude/worktrees/

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Agent-tool files, not project documentation.
# `next dev` writes apps/web/AGENTS.md itself (see
# node_modules/next/dist/server/lib/generate-agent-files.js) and re-creates it on
# every run, and CLAUDE.md is a one-line pointer at it. Neither is written by a
# human or useful to someone reading this repository, so they stay untracked
# rather than shipping as documentation in a public repo. They will still appear
# in your working tree; that is expected and harmless.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
**/AGENTS.md
**/CLAUDE.md
